From 0396e175dbcceea76d662ce277d08ee3f56cec8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew <matthewhale@live.com.au>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:14:34 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 58/59] E as in XvT; destroyed AI craft break up as in XvT

E (OpenXvT flight.c FLIGHT_KEY_E): from the slot after the current target,
wrapping, the first craft flying normally (object kind 0) with working
systems whose AI is attacking the player (maneuver 12 or 23); none keeps
the target.

game.xvt_breakup ("Destroyed Craft", default on), XvT collide 0x41FC50:
AI craft with a fuselage always break up (X-Wing blew a quarter up at
once): a wing on a random side comes off and the wreck recoils half its
deflection and tumbles 1-11 s. Craft without a fuselage tumble 8-15 s with
a random roll direction. Hits from large craft or on a stopped craft still
explode at once. The player's own death is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
